  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR covers parts 2-4 of #832: editing a placed mod vise pair, re-fitting it, and the follow-ups from the #833 review. Part 1, the dual-station block, is **not** in it. Why is under \"Held back\" below.\n\n**New undoable commands** (`crates/app/src/commands/mod_vise_edit.rs`), one undo step each:\n- **`SetModJaw`** changes a placed jaw block's figures, its insert, and, on an adjustable block, its slide. It regenerates the block's solid through `UpdateModel`, as `SetVise` does, and swaps the marker in the same step. The block stays on its hole and turn. It is refused by name when:\n  - the edit would change the block's side;\n  - a figure breaks the block law;\n  - a bolt or pin would land off the grid where the block stands (new `modvise::fit::footprint_at`);\n  - the block would hang off the plate (the plate seat check);\n  - the clamping face would reach into the stock.\n\n  A jaw lifted off the stock is a warning.\n- **`RefitModVise`** re-fits the adjustable block to the stock as it stands now. It runs the same `fit_pair` the pair was placed with, with the fixed block where it stands, and re-picks the adjustable block's hole and slide. Every refusal of the fit is passed on by name, and nothing moves.\n  - `RefitModVise::to_partner` finds the single fixed jaw block on the same plate. If there are none, or several, it refuses and names them.\n\n**Follow-ups from the #833 review:**\n- `SetPlate`'s jaw check now goes through `judge_face`, which `SetModJaw` shares. A face that was not in front of the stock before the edit (`face_gap == None`) counts as clear. The reviewer's probe used to pass with only a warning and is now refused: the stock moved +130 mm in X, then one plate edit (pitch X +10, pitch Y -2) puts the adjustable jaw 16 mm into it.\n- `mcp_plate` now asserts the `warning` field that `set_fixture_plate` returns (null when clear). `mcp_mod_vise` pins a non-null warning: a plate edit that lifts the fixed jaw 2 mm off the stock.\n\n**MCP tools** (`crates/app/src/mcp/modvise_tools.rs`):\n- `set_mod_jaw {name, figures{..., slide}, insert}` returns the block and its `warning`.\n- `refit_mod_vise {adjustable, fixed?}` returns the hole, turn, location, slide, opening, fixed_gap and warning.\n\n**UI:** each jaw block's row on the Fixtures page now has:\n- \"Edit jaw block…\" with body height, jaw height, jaw thickness, face offset, slide (adjustable block only), soft jaw, and a \"Set figures\" button that queues `SetModJaw`;\n- \"Re-fit to stock\" on the adjustable block, which queues `RefitModVise`.\n\nWarnings go through `with_warning` into the status line.\n\n**Save/load:** no new key. Both commands write only the existing `mod_jaw` and `on_plate` fields, which #830's lenient `fixture_keys` reader already loads (through `modvise_dto`). Old files load unchanged.\n\n**Decision record:** `docs/decisions/832-mod-vise-edit-refit.md`\n\n## Held back: the dual-station block (part 1)\nA dual-station block clamps two workpieces. A setup holds one stock, and fixtures are judged per setup (`fixture::tagged`). There are two ways to give the second station a stock, and both break the Prime Directive:\n- Take the second station's stock from another setup. That setup's program would never see the vise steel, so a gouge would go unflagged.\n- Put a copy of the steel in each setup. The copies then clash with each other.\n\nLeaving the second station empty is not \"fitted per station\". This needs a multi-stock design decision first (effort:max or research). #832 stays open for it (`Refs #832`).\n\n## How tested\nPinning tests:\n- `crates/app/tests/mod_vise_edit.rs` (new):\n  - `a_figure_edit_regenerates_the_block_where_it_stands_in_one_undo`\n  - `a_figure_edit_is_refused_by_name_and_a_lifted_jaw_warns`\n  - `a_refit_after_the_stock_changed_re_picks_the_hole_and_slide_in_one_undo` (three stock depths: H16, J16, I16; face on the stock to 1e-6; undo and redo exact to the bit)\n  - `a_refit_that_cannot_fit_is_refused_by_name_and_nothing_moves`\n  - `a_plate_edit_that_brings_a_jaw_into_a_stock_it_was_beside_is_refused` (the #833 probe; it fails with the old `None`-skip in place)\n  - `an_edited_and_re_fitted_pair_survives_a_save`\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_mod_vise.rs`: `a_placed_pair_is_edited_and_re_fitted_over_mcp`\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_plate.rs`: the `warning` field assertion.\n- Structural UI twin, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/fixture_modvise_tests.rs`:\n  - `a_jaw_block_row_edits_its_figures_in_one_undoable_step`\n  - `the_adjustable_row_re_fits_the_block_to_a_changed_stock`\n  - `a_refused_refit_is_named_in_the_status`\n\nGates on the final head (c4cab3dc), Linux:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (app suites 581 s, mcp_plate, ui suites 60 s; 0 failed). It covered mod_vise, mod_vise_edit, mod_vise_plate, mcp_mod_vise, mcp_plate, fixtures, fixture_plate*, fixture_keys_lenient, project_roundtrip and the ui lib.\n- `cargo test --test fixture_law_gaps`: ok (3).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate test a_plate_edit_that_brings_a_jaw_into_a_stock_it_was_beside_is_refused`: ok.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The dual-station block (held back, above).\n- Re-fitting with `MountAt::Dowels`. Jaw blocks are only ever placed on holes, so that case is refused by name and not fitted.\n- Re-fitting a pair turned 90 or 270 degrees is covered only through `fit_pair`'s existing quarter-turn tests, not by its own test.\n- No snapshot PNG was changed.\n\nChangelog: Mod vises: a placed jaw block's figures can be edited (`SetModJaw`, MCP `set_mod_jaw`) and the adjustable block re-fitted to a changed stock (`RefitModVise`, MCP `refit_mod_vise`), one undo each; a plate edit that brings a jaw from beside the stock into it is now refused (#832)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\nFork synced at v0.18.0 (branch cut from upstream main e0cb0049, the v0.18.0 release merge) (branch cut from upstream/main at e0cb0049, v0.18.0 release merge)\n\nRefs #832\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
